        <mxCell id="zNNUxuH0RXOb034LeN5t-630" value="&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 0in; font-family: &amp;quot;Comic Sans MS&amp;quot;; font-size: 40px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 40px;&quot;&gt;Scenarios (45min)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 0in; font-family: &amp;quot;Comic Sans MS&amp;quot;; font-size: 40px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 40px;&quot;&gt;.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 0in; font-family: &amp;quot;Comic Sans MS&amp;quot;; font-size: 40px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 40px;&quot;&gt;Single Region&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 0in; font-family: &amp;quot;Comic Sans MS&amp;quot;; font-size: 40px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 40px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;1. On-Prem Connectivity Using Global Reach, Forced Tunneling&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 0in; font-family: &amp;quot;Comic Sans MS&amp;quot;; font-size: 40px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 40px;&quot;&gt;2. Secured vWAN HUB Design with Routing Intent&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 0in; font-family: &amp;quot;Comic Sans MS&amp;quot;; font-size: 40px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 40px;&quot;&gt;3. Network Virtual Appliance (NVA) in AVS using NSX-T segments&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 0in; font-family: &amp;quot;Comic Sans MS&amp;quot;; font-size: 40px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 40px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 0in; font-family: &amp;quot;Comic Sans MS&amp;quot;; font-size: 40px;&quot;&gt;4. Network Virtual Appliance (NVA) in Azure VNET (with ARS)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 0in; font-family: &amp;quot;Comic Sans MS&amp;quot;; font-size: 40px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 40px;&quot;&gt;5. Transit VNET design with NVA in Azure NVET (with ARS)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 0in; font-family: &amp;quot;Comic Sans MS&amp;quo